    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0906" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg824"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 405.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 2, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your despatch of the 9th of
                    February, No. 268, and I have placed it with pleasure upon the records of the
                    department. It shows that you have compromised no part of the position of this
                    government in your conversation with Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys, and I notice with
                    satisfaction the friendly spirit with which he accepts your explanation. It is
                    hardly necessary to say that the misapprehensions which you have now corrected
                    excited no particular uneasiness here.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
